{'_client': <twikit.client.client.Client object at 0x000001E534E2AE40>, '_data': {'__typename': 'Tweet', 'rest_id': '1882091061734220104', 'core': {'user_results': {'result': {'__typename': 'User', 'id': 'VXNlcjoxMzAwMjA0OTU3MTM2ODA5OTg0', 'rest_id': '1300204957136809984', 'affiliates_highlighted_label': {}, 'has_graduated_access': True, 'is_blue_verified': True, 'profile_image_shape': 'Circle', 'legacy': {'can_dm': False, 'can_media_tag': False, 'created_at': 'Sun Aug 30 22:53:30 +0000 2020', 'default_profile': True, 'default_profile_image': False, 'description': 'GenX, Independent, Vet, will block 🤡’s.', 'entities': {'description': {'urls': []}}, 'fast_followers_count': 0, 'favourites_count': 389236, 'followers_count': 6028, 'friends_count': 584, 'has_custom_timelines': True, 'is_translator': False, 'listed_count': 5, 'location': 'United States', 'media_count': 22477, 'name': 'StopBSWokeCulture 🇺🇸', 'normal_followers_count': 6028, 'pinned_tweet_ids_str': ['1647772935304916992'], 'possibly_sensitive': False, 'profile_banner_url': 'https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/1300204957136809984/1640999222', 'profile_image_url_https': 'https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1496251000851734528/FNHMFS4Y_normal.jpg', 'profile_interstitial_type': '', 'screen_name': 'MkayUokay', 'statuses_count': 212824, 'translator_type': 'none', 'verified': False, 'want_retweets': False, 'withheld_in_countries': []}, 'professional': {'rest_id': '1589027189747597313', 'professional_type': 'Creator', 'category': [{'id': 511, 'name': 'Life Coach', 'icon_name': 'IconBriefcaseStroke'}]}}}}, 'unmention_data': {}, 'edit_control': {'edit_tweet_ids': ['1882091061734220104'], 'editable_until_msecs': '1737564051000', 'is_edit_eligible': False, 'edits_remaining': '5'}, 'is_translatable': False, 'views': {'count': '11', 'state': 'EnabledWithCount'}, 'source': '<a href="http://twitter.com/#!/download/ipad" rel="nofollow">Twitter for iPad</a>', 'note_tweet': {'is_expandable': True, 'note_tweet_results': {'result': {'id': 'Tm90ZVR3ZWV0OjE4ODIwOTEwNjE0ODI1Mjg3Njg=', 'text': "The Soviets thought they could replace farmers and direct plants to grow according to good Soviet management. Millions died and actual scientists were shot if they disagreed. \n\nEllison pushes the updated version. He also changes his tune depending on the audience. \n\n**Summary of Lysenkoism:**\n\nLysenkoism refers to the pseudo-scientific agricultural practices and biological theories promoted by Trofim Lysenko during the Stalinist period in the Soviet Union. Lysenko, who was not formally trained in genetics or biology, rose to prominence with his claims that:\n\n- Plants could be made to adapt to any environment by changing their conditions (vernalization).\n- Inheritance of acquired characteristics was possible, thus rejecting Mendelian genetics and Darwinian evolution in favor of Lamarckian ideas.\n\nLysenko's theories were politically motivated to align with Soviet ideology, emphasizing the environment over genetics, which was seen as bourgeois science. His approach promised quick solutions to agricultural problems, especially during times of food scarcity, but it ultimately led to disastrous agricultural results:\n\n- **Rejection of Scientific Genetics:** Lysenko's influence led to the suppression of genetic research in the Soviet Union. Scientists who opposed him, like Nikolai Vavilov, were imprisoned, persecuted, or executed. Vavilov himself died in prison in 1943.\n\n- **Agricultural Failures:** His practices, like close planting and deep sowing, often resulted in poor harvests. The rejection of hybrid vigor and selective breeding led to decreased crop yields at a time when the Soviet Union needed to feed a growing population.\n\n- **Economic and Food Crises:** The agricultural policies based on Lysenkoism contributed significantly to food shortages, famines, and economic setbacks. \n\n**Casualties Associated with Lysenkoism:**\n\nDetermining the exact number of deaths directly attributable to Lysenkoism is challenging due to the indirect nature of its impact:\n\n- **Starvation:** The most direct consequence was through famines, particularly during the 1930s and 1940s. While not the sole cause, Lysenko's agricultural policies exacerbated food shortages. Estimates vary, but some sources suggest that millions died due to famine conditions that were worsened by these misguided agricultural practices. For instance:\n  - The Soviet famine of 1932-1933 (Holodomor in Ukraine), where Lysenko's methods were implemented, resulted in millions of deaths, though this was also influenced by collectivization policies and other factors.\n\n- **Persecution of Scientists:** While the number of scientists killed directly due to Lysenkoism isn't precisely documented, many were imprisoned or executed. Nikolai Vavilov's death is one documented case. Historians estimate that several dozen to possibly hundreds of scientists faced severe repercussions.\n\n- **Long-term Impact:** Beyond immediate deaths, the suppression of genetics research delayed Soviet agriculture and science for decades, impacting food security and health, which might indirectly have led to further mortality over time.\n\nIn conclusion, while it's hard to attribute an exact number of deaths solely to Lysenkoism, it contributed to significant human suffering, including millions from famine, and the persecution of scientific communities. The total impact on human life would require considering both direct and indirect effects over several decades.", 'entity_set': {'hashtags': [], 'symbols': [], 'urls': [], 'user_mentions': []}}}}, 'legacy': {'bookmark_count': 0, 'bookmarked': False, 'created_at': 'Wed Jan 22 15:40:51 +0000 2025', 'conversation_id_str': '1881840343882293585', 'display_text_range': [14, 293], 'entities': {'hashtags': [], 'symbols': [], 'timestamps': [], 'urls': [], 'user_mentions': [{'id_str': '69156861', 'name': 'Chief Nerd', 'screen_name': 'TheChiefNerd', 'indices': [0, 13]}]}, 'favorite_co